\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For function fields K/k and L/l of transcendence degree at least two over algebraically closed characteristic-p fields, set $V_F=F^times/(F^times)^p$. Does the degree-one/degree-two Milnor product modulo p identify field isomorphisms carrying constants to constants bijectively with product-compatible $F_p-linear$ maps $V_K->V_L$ modulo one common $F_p^times$ scalar?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For function fields K/k and L/l of transcendence degree at least two over algebraically closed characteristic-p fields, set $V_F=F^times/(F^times)^p$. Does the degree-one/degree-two Milnor product modulo p identify field isomorphisms carrying constants to constants bijectively with product-compatible $F_p-linear$ maps $V_K->V_L$ modulo one common $F_p^times$ scalar?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2014/49}.
\item[S2] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2018/25}.
\item[S3] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Reconstruction-from-Milnor-K-theory-modulo-the-characteristic-October-5-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

