\section*{Milnor K reconstruction at the characteristic prime}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 009; 2026-10-05), the asserted result is that Milnor $K$-theory modulo the characteristic recovers such function fields from degree-two Steinberg relations, up to one nonzero scalar.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 009; 2026-10-05), vanishing symbols are interpreted through derivations over the subfield of $p$th powers. An intersection calculation recovers projective lines; one common power correction aligns these lines, and projective incidence gives the field operations.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result uses Milnor relations modulo the characteristic to reconstruct the field up to a common nonzero scalar. Complete coverage of the precise reconstruction correspondence in this record is not established by this catalogue, so the claim remains partial.

\subsection{Formal verification}
No Lean formalization is listed at this snapshot for manuscript 1 (family 009; 2026-10-05).

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

